{"timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:44:44.711Z","ordinal":842,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19ecc-82f0-7492-9f12-a328e4f8c843","turn_id":"01a1aa05-db10-7b43-a5dd-08621c7f8eb1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b6367978b0706f9016aec09ba18ec87d08bbed9a232ef43de","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Extend `sun shell-init` to wrap `gh`, just as it wraps `git`:\n\n1. Run the real `gh pr create`.\n2. If creation succeeds, run `sun pr --update` against the newly created PR.\n3. If coverage updating fails, warn without treating PR creation as failed.\n\nThen successful `git push` calls can refresh coverage on an existing PR.\n\nThis would cover commands run through the shell integration. PRs created through GitHub’s website would need a separate GitHub Actions workflow."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793853882086,"completed_at_ms":1793853884711}}
